  "notes": "Site is Squarespace; no bot check or captcha was hit, about 20 pages read. Logo is the header logo (navy round wave) at its original size, which loads as WebP. Hero is ExperienceCoffinBay141221-436, from the operator's own December 2021 shoot, also used on the Contact page. Gallery and trip photos are the shoot files named ExperienceCoffinBay141221-N and 20211214-DJI_N (drone, 1080 wide), plus RB1-3.jpg and ECB7.jpg from the home page. The Chris and Linda portrait (_DSC9407.jpg) is last in the gallery. Left out on purpose: the five award and membership badge graphics on the home and logos pages (TiCSA, EYR, Sustainable Tourism, TTT Winners); the eight 'image-asset.jpeg' files in the home page slideshow, which are social post graphics with sale text (one alt text mentions a Black Friday voucher sale) and vertical phone clips; the two square tour cards Experience-Coffin-Bay-Farm+Bay-Tour-NEW.jpg and Experience-Coffin-Bay-Short+Sweet-Tour-NEW.jpg (2601 by 2601), which look like designed graphics and could not be viewed; the page header images Web+1-1.jpg, Web+2-1.jpg and Web+7-1.jpg (2048 wide), which are probably plain photos but could not be checked for printed text; Hunter+Gatherer+Day-4.jpg, the home page hero, whose source is unclear; PTK_SEAFOOD-0019.jpg (About Us) and PCBO_web-0006.jpg (Vouchers), whose names suggest another business; the three phone photos of the boat being built in 2020 and a 2018 Tasting Australia screenshot. Video: the only video found is the YouTube background video on the home page hero (DcGP2-KhpcE), recorded as the operator's own because it is part of its home page, but its content and channel were not checked. Left out: the Tasting Australia video on the 2018 blog post (YouTube vYbvAUg8tFY), which the site credits to another videographer and Alliance Airlines. The site links no YouTube or Vimeo channel."
